  "body": "Parent: #6022 (placement policy). Related: #5981/#5983 (Atlas docs migration), #6267 (note_submission pilot), #3125 (provenance registry).\n\nApply #6022's placement rules to the durable, non-document agent-note remainder in `~/workspace/research_notes/` and completed `~/workspace/goals/**` workspaces. This is not a second Atlas documentation sweep and does not authorize bulk migration of memory.\n\n## Scope\n- Exclude every document already enumerated by #5981 and all sandbox-environment material classified STAY by #5983.\n- Inventory only candidate durable findings and decisions outside that docs-migration batch. Record source path, content hash, owner, sensitivity, provenance, and recommended canonical home (repo doc, Zettelkasten, ID-native candidate, or retain locally).\n- Treat `~/memory/` as reference-only: do not bulk read, copy, ingest, or delete memory topics. Record only pointers needed to make that boundary explicit.\n- For accepted migrations, copy through the note_submission staging/review flow, preserve the original, and add a canonical pointer where the source is maintained.\n\n## Acceptance\n- A reviewable manifest distinguishes classified candidates from scratch, active goal logs, sandbox-only material, and memory.\n- Every migrated entry has an explicit canonical owner, provenance/hash, sensitivity decision, and source pointer; uncertain items remain unmoved and staged.\n- No historical source is deleted; no content is published to a Zettelkasten corpus or Atlas tier without human promotion.\n- The manifest and promotion results are checked against #6022's decision table and #5981/#5983's classification, with duplicates and exclusions called out.\n\n## Dependencies\nBlocked by #6022 placement design review/merge and coordination with the #5981/#5983 migration classification. Reuse #6267's submission path; this issue does not change its envelope or ID publication format.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every candidate durable finding/decision in the named trees, outside the #5981/#5983 exclusions, appears in the inventory with source path, content hash, owner, sensitivity, provenance, and a recommended canonical home.\n- `~/memory/` is treated as reference-only: pointers recorded where needed, no bulk read/copy/ingest/delete.\n- Each accepted migration goes through the note_submission staging/review flow, preserves the original, and leaves a canonical pointer at the maintained source.\n- The exclusion set (the #5981 batch and #5983 STAY material) is listed explicitly so the sweep's boundary is auditable.\n",
